<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36679" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plinthis</span></b> , ĭdis,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλινθίς</span> (a square
		tile). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A square;</i> in architect., <i>a
				square base</i>, <i>a plinth</i>, for plinthus,
				<i><span class="en">Vitr.
				3, 3, 2</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in land-surveying, for plinthus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hyg. Condit. Agror. p. 210</span></i>
			 Goes.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Plur.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plinthĭ-des</span></b> , <i>a register</i>
			in the hydraulic organ, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 10, 8, 8</span></i>; v.
		pleuritis.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
